IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ip-nouns`
IMPORT `ip-framework`
IMPORT `ip-restraints`
IMPORT `ip-safety-zone`

-- POSITIVE CONTROLS. Every assertion in this file is WRONG on purpose, and must FAIL.
-- check.sh expects exactly this many failures here (and none anywhere else), so a build
-- that stopped evaluating assertions, or a rule that stopped distinguishing these cases,
-- turns the check red. Each states a misreading of the guidelines that the encoding must
-- not make.

§ `Positive controls: each assertion must fail`

`no transfer` MEANS `Transfer of intellectual property rights (5.7)` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

`a restraint that is not facially anticompetitive` MEANS `Restraint in a licensing arrangement` OF `a type of restraint not accorded per se treatment`, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE

GIVEN markets IS A LIST OF `Relevant market significantly affected by the restraint`
      wider IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Licensing arrangement before the safety zone (4.3)`
`a patent license affecting` MEANS `Licensing arrangement before the safety zone (4.3)` OF `a patent`, TRUE, TRUE, `no transfer`, `a restraint that is not facially anticompetitive`, wider, markets

`inside` MEANS JUST `inside the safety zone: absent extraordinary circumstances, the agencies will not challenge the restraint`

-- WRONG: 20.01 percent is not "no more than twenty percent".
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`a patent license affecting` (LIST `Relevant market significantly affected by the restraint` OF "widgets", `a goods market`, JUST (`Market shares of the licensor and its licensees` OF 20.01, EMPTY), EMPTY, EMPTY) FALSE) EQUALS `inside`

-- WRONG: three independently controlled technologies are not "four or more".
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`a patent license affecting` (LIST `Relevant market significantly affected by the restraint` OF "T", `a technology market`, NOTHING, (LIST (`Other technology` OF "T1", "C1", FALSE, TRUE), (`Other technology` OF "T2", "C2", FALSE, TRUE), (`Other technology` OF "T3", "C3", FALSE, TRUE)), EMPTY) TRUE) EQUALS `inside`

-- WRONG: a per se type that contributes to an efficiency-enhancing integration is judged
-- under the rule of reason (3.4), not challenged per se.
#ASSERT `3.4: the mode of analysis` (`Restraint in a licensing arrangement` OF `market division among horizontal competitors`, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS `the agencies will challenge the restraint under the per se rule`

-- WRONG: without market power in the tying product, 5.3 does not say the agencies would be
-- likely to challenge a tie, whatever protects the tying item.
#ASSERT `5.3: tying` (`Tying facts (5.3)` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the agencies would be likely to challenge the tying arrangement`
